  "name": "Example: Finding the Complement of an Intersection",
  "problem": "If $\\overline{P} = \\{ 2, 4, 6 \\}$ and $\\overline{Q} = \\{ 1, 2, 4 \\},$ then what is $\\overline{ P \\cap Q }?$",
  "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for intersections states that\n\n$$\n\\overline{P \\cap Q} \\equiv \\overline{P} \\cup \\overline{Q}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{P\\cap Q} & =\\overset{\u2015}{P}\\cup \\overset{\u2015}{Q} \\\\  & ={2,4,6}\\cup {1,2,4} \\\\  & ={1,2,4,6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
